Most warlocks use the Voidwalker because it provides **sustain and safety** while leveling: **Consume Shadows** lets them recover health without eating/drinking, and **Torment/Suffering** tank mobs so the warlock can DoT and wand without taking damage. The Succubus deals more damage and has **Seduction**, but it requires more micromanagement, doesn't hold threat well, and offers no out-of-combat regeneration—making the Voidwalker the more efficient, lower-maintenance choice for most players. [end of text]


